87
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:25,830
I've found her.

88
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,270
So it's her.

89
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,360
I'm off.

90
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:23,030
[Study Hard]

91
00:05:29,950 --> 00:05:31,000
Dating is simple.

92
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:31,500
[How does dating usually progress?]

93
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:34,420
Confess your feelings, go on dates,
and hold hands.

94
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,310
And then comes the next big step:

95
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:44,270
kissing.

96
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,360
Kissing is a natural stage
in every relationship.

97
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:51,159
If you haven't even kissed,
you can hardly call yourselves a couple.

98
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:21,260
I want a kiss too.

99
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,159
Xiangxiang.

100
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:34,950
Hello.

101
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,430
You just can't help it, you know.

102
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,870
Totally normal between couples, right?

103
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:06,640
By the way, have you and Gu Han...

104
00:07:10,590 --> 00:07:11,470
No.

105
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,610
Then you two are moving way too slowly.

106
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,680
Well, I'm a girl, after all.

107
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:19,760
You can take the initiative
and create opportunities.

108
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,640
[Books: The Key to Wisdom]

109
00:07:42,159 --> 00:07:43,830
Can you help me find a book?

110
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:44,950
What book?

111
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:48,510
"Selected Chinese Literary Works
Through the Ages."

112
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:50,040
It should be over there somewhere.

113
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,870
But I just can't find it.

114
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,190
Sure.

115
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,000
Here.

116
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,050
What's the title again?

117
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:07,600
"Selected Chinese Literary Works
Through the Ages."

118
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:30,490
Are you sure

119
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,669
no one else has checked it out?

120
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,610
[Selected Chinese Literary Works
Through the Ages]

121
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,030
I checked the records.

122
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,490
It's still in the library.

123
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:48,430
Then I'll go ask about it.

124
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:33,740
Sorry, sorry.

125
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:56,800
"Selected Chinese Literary Works...

126
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:04,080
Through the Ages..."

127
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,410
I don't quite understand this one.

128
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:33,280
This question?

129
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:41,170
This one's actually pretty simple.

130
00:10:41,170 --> 00:10:42,500
Basically, economics

131
00:10:42,530 --> 00:10:45,070
uses statistics to analyze data.

132
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,270
And there are 2 main types of analysis:

133
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:48,600
descriptive and inferential.

134
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,600
Then we can present the results

135
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:53,120
using tables, graphs,

136
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,320
or numerical values.

137
00:11:05,550 --> 00:11:06,270
Then...

138
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:47,840
Le Xiaotao!

139
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:57,080
Thank you for treating me to a meal.

140
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,120
I didn't really help you with anything.

141
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,000
Not at all.

142
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,080
If it weren't for you,

143
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,000
those 2 haters
would've beaten me up by now.

144
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,660
It was no big deal. No big deal.

145
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,720
I know where those haters came from.

146
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,750
Where?

147
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,480
I interviewed with
an influencer agency before.

148
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,270
I wouldn't go along with the image
they wanted me to project,

149
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,550
so they got people to smear me online.

150
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:15,030
I've already reported them to the police.

151
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:16,090
You reported them?

152
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,090
You think I was wrong to do that?

153
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,550
No, no, no.

154
00:12:19,750 --> 00:12:20,910
I just wonder

155
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:22,760
whether petty people like that

156
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:25,240
might try to come after you in other ways.

157
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,390
They won't.

158
00:12:29,030 --> 00:12:30,510
Can you stop following me around?

159
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:32,000
You're so annoying!

160
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:39,600
I already have a boyfriend.

161
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,000
Don't follow me anymore.

162
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:46,860
Stay away from my girlfriend!

163
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:48,020
Did you hear me?

164
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,360
Let's go.

165
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:52,870
Let's go.

166
00:12:53,710 --> 00:12:54,430
Ignore him.

167
00:12:55,870 --> 00:12:57,810
All departments, get ready.

168
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:57,840
[The Starry Sky]

169
00:12:57,870 --> 00:12:59,840
[24s]

170
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:01,080
Three, two, one, go!

171
00:12:59,930 --> 00:13:05,950
[The Starry Sky]

172
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,510
Jump your way.

173
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:03,720
Shoot for your dreams.

174
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:06,240
Welcome to 24s, a special program
brought to you by The Starry Sky.

175
00:13:06,010 --> 00:13:09,550
[24s]

176
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:08,360
Today, we'd like to
introduce a new friend:

177
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:11,020
Zhou Xiangxiang, the new host of "24s."

178
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,270
Hello, everyone.

179
00:13:12,270 --> 00:13:13,840
I'm Zhou Xiangxiang,

180
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,000
the new host of "24s."

181
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,320
I'll be here on "24s"

182
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:18,550
as we enjoy basketball together.

183
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,150
I'm sorry.

184
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:29,010
I had to make up an excuse just now.

185
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:31,270
Do you influencers often get harassed

186
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:32,930
by mindless haters like that?

187
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:36,630
I'll explain everything to you later.

188
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:37,240
Then...

189
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,360
how about I walk you back?

190
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:49,260
[Starry Sky]

191
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:02,960
Well? How was that?

192
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,550
I did okay just now, right?

193
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:05,410
Perfect score.

194
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,550
I just checked.

195
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:08,610
Everyone online is praising you.

196
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:10,270
You have no idea

197
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:12,530
how nervous I was during the live stream.

198
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:13,670
Good thing I didn't mess anything up.

199
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:15,270
And my boss even praised me.

200
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,400
Are you tired?

201
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,540
I'll take you back.

202
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:34,580
[Starry Sky]

203
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,390
Dorm Supervisor?

204
00:14:51,910 --> 00:14:53,710
Dorm Supervisor, are you there?

205
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:01,150
Dorm Supervisor!

206
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,120
It's too late.

207
00:15:04,410 --> 00:15:05,140
How about...

208
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:07,750
you stay at my place tonight?

209
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:10,860
I have a guest room.

210
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:18,150
Let's go.

211
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:38,980
Come in.

212
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,580
Here're the slippers.

213
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,450
Just leave your shoes here.

214
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:56,180
Have a seat.

215
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,530
I'll get the room ready.

216
00:16:03,390 --> 00:16:04,270
Are you hungry?

217
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:06,600
A little.

218
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,500
I'll fix you something to eat.

219
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:29,270
Here.

220
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,480
Try my deluxe instant noodles.

221
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,750
See if they're better than the ones

222
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,660
we had during our research trip.

223
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:37,260
Here.

224
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:43,720
A fried egg?

225
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:47,140
And a boiled egg?

226
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:49,970
I wasn't sure which kind you liked,

227
00:16:49,970 --> 00:16:50,770
so I made both.

228
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:55,310
What am I, a pig?

229
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:00,440
Here.

230
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,410
They're so good!

231
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:16,579
Have some soup.

232
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,920
You have some too.

233
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:25,790
Okay.

234
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,440
Is the power out?

235
00:18:21,330 --> 00:18:22,740
Yes, I...

236
00:18:23,510 --> 00:18:26,400
forgot there was
a scheduled power outage today.

237
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,680
Okay.

238
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:35,650
You have candles at home, right?

239
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,110
Yes.

240
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,040
You can sleep in my room tonight.

241
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,700
What's inside the box?

242
00:19:02,310 --> 00:19:04,640
These are all things from your childhood.

243
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:06,750
This one is mine.

244
00:19:10,110 --> 00:19:11,040
A piece of chalk?

245
00:19:13,070 --> 00:19:14,160
Do you remember when your class was

246
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,560
working on a blackboard display in school?

247
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:18,750
Everyone else in your class had left.

248
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:20,160
You were too short to reach,

249
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,750
so I lifted you up,
and you drew a tree up there.

250
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:24,640
Was I really that short?

251
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,090
What about this one?

252
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:32,100
Do you remember
that bicycle you had as a kid?

253
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,590
This is the little light from that bike.

254
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,830
You were small and couldn't ride well yet,

255
00:19:36,830 --> 00:19:38,890
so I pushed you from behind every day.

256
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:46,640
What about this one?

257
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:50,110
When you were little,
you dragged me to the park...

258
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:51,030
I remember.

259
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:52,960
I remember.

260
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:37,920
When did you start liking me?

261
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:48,750
Since...

262
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:51,810
I found out you were Zhou Xiangxiang.

263
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:54,160
That's when it started.

264
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,850
I'm a bit sleepy now.

265
00:21:31,770 --> 00:21:32,700
Go to sleep then.

266
00:22:26,070 --> 00:22:27,000
Still up?

267
00:22:36,270 --> 00:22:38,000
Then let me take you somewhere.

268
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,840
Now that I think about it,

269
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,650
everything you've done

270
00:23:29,750 --> 00:23:32,000
since we met again has been for my sake.

271
00:23:35,310 --> 00:23:37,640
I'm the one who didn't remember anything.

272
00:23:38,350 --> 00:23:40,350
Knowing you've liked me for so long,

273
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,270
I'm really happy.

274
00:23:45,270 --> 00:23:47,200
And I feel incredibly lucky, too.

275
00:24:24,110 --> 00:24:24,720
A cat.

276
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:41,760
♪ Time circles round, going nowhere ♪

277
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:47,160
♪ We once met, then passed each other by ♪

278
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:56,070
♪ Eyes closed, memories quietly unfold ♪

279
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:03,390
♪ Every story will unfold ♪

280
00:25:04,390 --> 00:25:10,790
♪ I look up and see the sleepless stars ♪

281
00:25:11,710 --> 00:25:15,890
♪ So this is what it means to miss you ♪

282
00:25:16,410 --> 00:25:24,910
♪ I want you to say those words at last ♪

283
00:25:25,570 --> 00:25:30,330
♪ Love means being with you ♪

284
00:25:30,620 --> 00:25:33,580
♪ I love you ♪

285
00:25:34,270 --> 00:25:37,390
♪ I miss you ♪

286
00:25:38,290 --> 00:25:45,030
♪ The me who met you that day
belongs to long, long ago ♪

287
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:20,030
Why didn't you make a sound
when you came in?

288
00:26:20,030 --> 00:26:22,350
I was afraid of disturbing your training.

289
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:24,210
How have you been feeling lately?

290
00:26:27,350 --> 00:26:29,410
Not so good. I don't have much energy.

291
00:26:30,030 --> 00:26:31,200
No energy?

292
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:34,030
Then I'll buy you a lot of fitness meals,

293
00:26:34,030 --> 00:26:36,160
plus yogurt and bananas to refuel you.

294
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,940
That's not how you refuel.

295
00:26:40,790 --> 00:26:42,070
Then how?

296
00:27:07,350 --> 00:27:08,200
Like this.

297
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,920
Who did you learn that from?

298
00:28:24,590 --> 00:28:25,110
Have one.

299
00:28:25,110 --> 00:28:25,720
Okay.

300
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:35,680
You have one too.

301
00:28:47,270 --> 00:28:49,750
What's going on with you two?

302
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:52,070
Nothing.

303
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:55,600
[Landlord]

304
00:28:58,920 --> 00:28:59,920
Hello, landlord.

305
00:29:02,030 --> 00:29:02,920
Xiangxiang.

306
00:29:03,830 --> 00:29:04,960
Come clean.

307
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:12,580
Do you want something to drink?
I'll go buy some.

308
00:29:13,440 --> 00:29:14,240
I'll go.

309
00:29:24,310 --> 00:29:25,920
Can I pay the rent just one month late?

310
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,820
I'm planning to
keep renting from you long-term.

311
00:29:27,820 --> 00:29:29,350
How about I pay 1,000 now

312
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:31,350
and definitely make up the rest
next month?

313
00:29:31,350 --> 00:29:32,590
Just give me one month.

314
00:29:32,590 --> 00:29:33,160
Hello...

315
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:35,680
Hello?

316
00:29:40,030 --> 00:29:40,830
What's wrong?

317
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:45,160
Nothing. I was just discussing
the rent with my landlord.

318
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:47,680
Your internship pays you a salary, right?

319
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:50,070
Yeah. So it's all sorted out.

320
00:29:51,550 --> 00:29:52,410
I want that one.

321
00:29:56,030 --> 00:29:56,720
Hello.

322
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,330
These 4, please.

323
00:30:11,970 --> 00:30:13,780
[Gu Han] [1500; Please accept]

324
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:17,830
It's a loan.

325
00:30:36,620 --> 00:30:37,620
[Canada; Study Abroad]

326
00:30:37,680 --> 00:30:38,610
[Recommended Business Programs
at Humber College]

327
00:30:41,010 --> 00:30:43,860
[Desautels Faculty of Management
at McGill University]

328
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:37,440
Auntie Wan!

329
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:41,660
Have a seat.

330
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:48,160
What did you want to see me about?

331
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:49,400
Tell me the truth.

332
00:31:50,310 --> 00:31:52,170
Are you hiding something from me?

333
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:01,410
Did you know Gu Han is seeing someone?

334
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:05,310
I found a portrait of a girl in his room.

335
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:07,210
I'd never seen it there before.

336
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:08,270
Really?

337
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:14,440
Xiangxiang,

338
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:17,160
could you help me
get some info out of Gu Han

339
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:18,480
and find out who she is?

340
00:32:21,350 --> 00:32:24,240
Actually, I think
you could just ask him directly.

341
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:28,030
I just want to know
what kind of girl she is.

342
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,640
Auntie Wan, you seem so curious.

343
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:33,750
Is it because you have
certain requirements

344
00:32:33,750 --> 00:32:34,960
for his girlfriend?

345
00:32:36,720 --> 00:32:38,720
Nothing in particular, really.

346
00:32:40,830 --> 00:32:42,690
I've thought about it myself too—

347
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:43,830
what

348
00:32:43,830 --> 00:32:46,000
kind of girl should Gu Han find?

349
00:32:48,750 --> 00:32:50,510
She should have long hair

350
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:54,040
and a master's degree or higher.

351
00:32:55,550 --> 00:32:57,000
It'd be best if she also studied finance

352
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,760
or business administration.

353
00:32:59,110 --> 00:33:01,110
After all, our family runs a business.

354
00:33:01,110 --> 00:33:03,960
She could help out in the future, right?

355
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,400
That sounds good. Really good.
